WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.350
Instructor: Okay, so let's talk about

00:01.350 --> 00:03.540
installing git on a Mac.

00:03.540 --> 00:07.110
Most Macs these days actually come with git pre-installed

00:07.110 --> 00:09.120
and normally that will work fine.

00:09.120 --> 00:11.010
However, this course is actually using

00:11.010 --> 00:12.870
some of the newer features in git,

00:12.870 --> 00:16.590
some new syntax that older versions don't contain.

00:16.590 --> 00:17.910
So you wanna make sure

00:17.910 --> 00:22.910
that you're using git 2.23, 2.23, 2.23 and above.

00:25.296 --> 00:28.770
And the easiest way to do that is to open up a terminal app.

00:28.770 --> 00:30.330
I'll just be using throughout this course

00:30.330 --> 00:33.060
the built-in terminal utility on a Mac.

00:33.060 --> 00:37.470
So it's in applications, utilities, terminal

00:37.470 --> 00:39.180
but I usually just search for it

00:39.180 --> 00:42.510
and honestly it's pretty much always open on my machine.

00:42.510 --> 00:44.940
Alright, so the command that we'll run

00:44.940 --> 00:49.020
to check our version is git --version.

00:49.020 --> 00:52.020
So I see 2.24.3.

00:52.020 --> 00:55.680
I really don't need to upgrade or update,

00:55.680 --> 00:58.030
but just to show you how to go through with it.

00:59.070 --> 01:00.900
If you go to the git documentation,

01:00.900 --> 01:02.910
the link I've included as a resource

01:02.910 --> 01:03.900
with this video

01:03.900 --> 01:05.280
and you click download,

01:05.280 --> 01:06.990
it will detect if you're on a Mac,

01:06.990 --> 01:09.360
download the latest version for Mac.

01:09.360 --> 01:12.540
So it looks like there's different types of releases.

01:12.540 --> 01:15.240
We're gonna click this one here, not the source release,

01:15.240 --> 01:17.493
but the release it's suggesting for Mac.

01:18.540 --> 01:21.750
Okay? And so nothing is gonna start installing just yet,

01:21.750 --> 01:25.680
but what we're gonna do next is click on binary installer.

01:25.680 --> 01:27.930
And you really don't need to worry about this

01:27.930 --> 01:29.760
and panic if things aren't going great.

01:29.760 --> 01:32.100
Remember, you already have git installed,

01:32.100 --> 01:35.940
and if you already have something above 2.23,

01:35.940 --> 01:37.590
then I wouldn't stress about it.

01:37.590 --> 01:39.832
The differences are all very, very minor.

01:39.832 --> 01:42.810
Probably have nothing to do with the videos in this course,

01:42.810 --> 01:44.430
but I'm gonna just show you how to do this.

01:44.430 --> 01:45.690
So we're gonna click this link where

01:45.690 --> 01:48.513
it says Tim Harper provides an installer for git.

01:50.175 --> 01:53.220
Okay. And then we're going to select the latest version here

01:53.220 --> 01:55.143
which for me is 2.27.

01:56.280 --> 01:58.443
And then we just wait for it to download.

01:59.719 --> 02:00.552
So there it is.

02:00.552 --> 02:02.010
And then we'll have to open that up.

02:02.010 --> 02:05.580
Here we are, we just double click on the package

02:05.580 --> 02:08.100
and then I'm gonna have to go into my system preferences

02:08.100 --> 02:09.450
and say, no, no, it's okay.

02:09.450 --> 02:10.950
Don't worry about this.

02:10.950 --> 02:13.770
So I'll go into the security and privacy tab

02:13.770 --> 02:15.450
of my system preferences,

02:15.450 --> 02:17.650
and then I'm going to click open anyway

02:19.710 --> 02:21.810
and then I'm gonna click open.

02:21.810 --> 02:25.110
Okay, now we make it to the installer.

02:25.110 --> 02:28.230
Continue, install,

02:28.230 --> 02:31.170
password or fingerprint depending on your Mac,

02:31.170 --> 02:33.030
and we'll wait a little bit.

02:33.030 --> 02:35.400
All right, it says installation was successful,

02:35.400 --> 02:37.260
we'll move it to the trash.

02:37.260 --> 02:40.830
Alright, so it may seem like our version has not changed,

02:40.830 --> 02:43.050
right? I run git --version again

02:43.050 --> 02:46.170
in my terminal it still says 2.24.3,

02:46.170 --> 02:47.400
but if I open a new window

02:47.400 --> 02:48.960
or even just a new tab,

02:48.960 --> 02:50.130
this is a new tab.

02:50.130 --> 02:51.900
If I run the same command,

02:51.900 --> 02:54.630
we now see we actually have the latest version.

02:54.630 --> 02:56.250
So you just need to open a new window,

02:56.250 --> 02:57.900
a new tab you can verify.

02:57.900 --> 03:00.510
Don't worry if you don't have exactly 2.27,

03:00.510 --> 03:03.480
just aim to have greater than 2.23.

03:03.480 --> 03:04.530
And even if you don't,

03:04.530 --> 03:06.330
the differences really will only come up

03:06.330 --> 03:08.190
with one or two commands,

03:08.190 --> 03:09.900
but it's pretty easy to install.

03:09.900 --> 03:12.360
Hopefully you don't run into any major issues.

03:12.360 --> 03:15.570
And if you do, we have TAs of course to help you out.

03:15.570 --> 03:17.460
But really it's just a package you install.

03:17.460 --> 03:19.110
The most annoying part these days on a Mac

03:19.110 --> 03:22.770
is clicking all of the security system preferences stuff.

03:22.770 --> 03:25.020
Alright, so we now have git installed.

03:25.020 --> 03:27.593
Next up I'm gonna talk about something called GitKraken.
